{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MolecularConstruction.SymmetricBlockDomainWeight","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MolecularConstruction.SymmetricBlockDomainWeight","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.List.Basic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.double_bond_weight_eq_q_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.double_bond_weight_eq_q_sq","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/symmetric-block-domain-weight.lean#L52-L57","doc":"**Double bond `= q²`.** A double bond (order 2) weighs `q²` — numerically\nthe lone/bond ratio — so on the symmetric block bond order increments the\nweight by one factor of `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.bond_order_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.bond_order_weight","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/symmetric-block-domain-weight.lean#L44-L50","doc":"**Bond-order weight.** A bond of order `k` — a length-`k` braid word\n`σ^k` — has weight `q^k` on the symmetric block (single `q`, double `q²`,\ntriple `q³`). Specialises `symmetric_block_domain_weight` to a constant word,\ngiving the general crystal/lattice domain-weight law. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.lone_bond_ratio_q_squared","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.lone_bond_ratio_q_squared","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/symmetric-block-domain-weight.lean#L38-L42","doc":"**Lone/bond ratio `= q²`.** The lone pair `e⁻ = σ₀σ₁σ₀` (length 3) has\nweight `q³`, the `σ`-bond (length 1) has weight `q`, so the lone-pair weight is\n`q²` times the bond weight: `q³ = q² · q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.symmetric_block_domain_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.symmetric_block_domain_weight","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/symmetric-block-domain-weight.lean#L28-L36","doc":"**Symmetric-block domain weight.** On the trivial representation (every\ngenerator `↦ q`), a domain given by a braid word `w` has weight `q ^ w.length`:\nthe product of the per-generator scalars `q` over the word. Proved by induction\non `w` (bedrock `List.prod_cons` / `pow_succ`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:symmetric-block-domain-weight","label":"prop:symmetric-block-domain-weight","md":"quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/symmetric-block-domain-weight.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}